        ":question/problem": "![](images/45/4534ed02abf6740df78c3285292e7235391bc76352e16cfdcd2a149dfc7046c4.png)\n\nWater is being pumped from tank $A$ to tank $B.$ The graph above shows the amount of water (in liters) in each tank as a function of time (in minutes). At what time do tanks $A$ and $B$ contain the same amount of water?\n\nThe tanks contain the same amount of water after{{field-1}}minutes.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The tanks contain the same amount when the two graphs intersect.\n\n![](images/23/23efe932ef71f93f3a455a93bda45ded7e44b059853308f6d760a4df4bc7d349.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(4,15).$ So, the tanks contain the same amount ($15\\,\\text{L}$) of water after $t=4$ minutes."
